§ `42 to 46. Judgments, orders and decrees`

`s42 a judgment barring a second suit` MEANS `Judgment Facts` WITH
    `the judgment, order or decree by law prevents a court from taking cognizance of a suit or holding a trial` IS TRUE
    `the question is whether the court ought to take cognizance of the suit or hold the trial` IS TRUE
    `the judgment, order or decree is a final one of a competent court in the exercise of probate, matrimonial, admiralty or bankruptcy jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `it confers on or takes away from a person a legal character, or declares a person entitled to a legal character or to a specific thing, not as against a specified person but absolutely` IS FALSE
    `the existence of that legal character, or the title of that person to that thing, is relevant` IS FALSE
    `the judgment, order or decree relates to matters of a public nature relevant to the inquiry` IS FALSE
    `the existence of the judgment, order or decree is a fact in issue` IS FALSE
    `the judgment, order or decree is relevant under another provision of the Act` IS FALSE
    `the judgment, order or decree is relevant under section 42, 43 or 44 and has been proved by the adverse party` IS FALSE
    `it was delivered by a court not competent to deliver it, or was obtained by fraud or collusion` IS FALSE

