§ `45A. Convictions and acquittals`

`s45A conviction relevant to an issue` MEANS `Conviction Facts` WITH
    `the person has been convicted or acquitted of an offence by or before a court in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the conviction or acquittal is relevant to an issue in the proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the person was convicted upon a plea of guilty` IS FALSE
    `the conviction is subject to review or appeal that has not yet been determined` IS FALSE
    `the conviction has been quashed or set aside` IS FALSE
    `a pardon has been given in respect of the conviction` IS FALSE
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `a written law or other rule of law provides that a conviction is not admissible to prove a tendency or disposition on the part of the accused to commit the kind of offence charged` IS FALSE
    `a certificate of conviction or acquittal is signed by the Registrar of the Supreme Court, the registrar of the State Courts or the registrar of the Family Justice Courts and gives the substance and effect of the charge and of the conviction or acquittal` IS FALSE

`s45A conviction on a plea of guilty` MEANS `Conviction Facts` WITH
