§ `47 to 53. Opinions`

`s47 an expert whose help the court needs` MEANS `Opinion Facts` WITH
    `the court is likely to derive assistance from an opinion upon a point of scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` IS TRUE
    `the person has scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience` IS TRUE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the opinion as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact supports or is inconsistent with a relevant opinion of an expert` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the person by whom a document was written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person acquainted with the handwriting of the person by whom the document is supposed to be written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinioner has seen that person write, or has received documents purporting to be written by that person in answer to documents written by the opinioner or under the opinioner's authority, or documents purporting to be written by that person have been habitually submitted to the opinioner in the ordinary course of business` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the existence of a general custom or right` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person who would be likely to know of its existence if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the usages and tenets of a body of men or family, the constitution and government of a religious or charitable foundation, or the meaning of words or terms used in particular districts or by particular classes of people` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person having special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the relationship of one person to another` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is expressed by conduct of a person who as a member of the family or otherwise has special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the prosecution is under section 6A of the Women's Charter 1961 and the question is whether there was a marriage` IS FALSE
    `the opinion of a living person is relevant` IS FALSE

`s47 an expert but not in the interests of justice` MEANS `Opinion Facts` WITH
    `the court is likely to derive assistance from an opinion upon a point of scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` IS TRUE
    `the person has scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience` IS TRUE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the opinion as relevant` IS TRUE
    `the fact supports or is inconsistent with a relevant opinion of an expert` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the person by whom a document was written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person acquainted with the handwriting of the person by whom the document is supposed to be written or signed` IS FALSE
    `the opinioner has seen that person write, or has received documents purporting to be written by that person in answer to documents written by the opinioner or under the opinioner's authority, or documents purporting to be written by that person have been habitually submitted to the opinioner in the ordinary course of business` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the existence of a general custom or right` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person who would be likely to know of its existence if it existed` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the usages and tenets of a body of men or family, the constitution and government of a religious or charitable foundation, or the meaning of words or terms used in particular districts or by particular classes of people` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is that of a person having special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the court has to form an opinion as to the relationship of one person to another` IS FALSE
    `the opinion is expressed by conduct of a person who as a member of the family or otherwise has special means of knowledge on the subject` IS FALSE
    `the prosecution is under section 6A of the Women's Charter 1961 and the question is whether there was a marriage` IS FALSE
    `the opinion of a living person is relevant` IS FALSE

`s47 no assistance to the court` MEANS `Opinion Facts` WITH
    `the court is likely to derive assistance from an opinion upon a point of scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` IS FALSE
    `the person has scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience` IS TRUE
    `the court is of the view that it would not be in the interests of justice to treat the opinion as relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact supports or is inconsistent with a relevant opinion of an expert` IS FALSE
