    `the accused called a witness to give evidence tending to establish that the accused is of good disposition or reputation` IS FALSE
    `the party seeking to call the evidence is the prosecution or a person jointly charged with the accused` IS FALSE
    `the accused has previous convictions` IS FALSE

`s57 expl particular acts` MEANS `Character Facts` WITH
    `the kind of proceedings` IS `criminal proceedings`
    `the fact is that the character of a person is such as to render probable or improbable conduct imputed to the person` IS TRUE
    `the character appears from facts otherwise relevant` IS FALSE
    `the fact is that the accused is of a good character` IS FALSE
    `the fact is that the character of a person is such as to affect the amount of damages the person ought to receive` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of general reputation and general disposition and not of particular acts by which reputation or disposition are shown` IS FALSE
    `the accused or the accused's advocate asked a witness questions with a view to establishing that the accused is of good disposition or reputation` IS FALSE
    `the accused gave evidence tending to establish that the accused is of good disposition or reputation` IS FALSE
    `the accused called a witness to give evidence tending to establish that the accused is of good disposition or reputation` IS FALSE
    `the party seeking to call the evidence is the prosecution or a person jointly charged with the accused` IS FALSE
    `the accused has previous convictions` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the form of the character evidence is permitted by the Explanation to section 57` `s57 expl general reputation`

#ASSERT NOT `the form of the character evidence is permitted by the Explanation to section 57` `s57 expl particular acts`

#ASSERT `the form of the character evidence is permitted by the Explanation to section 57` `s56 accused asks witnesses about good character; prosecution responds`
